          "value": "pass"
        },
        "shell": "/usr/bin/pwpolicy -getaccountpolicies 2> /dev/null | /usr/bin/tail +2 | /usr/bin/xmllint --xpath '//dict/key[text()=\"autoEnableInSeconds\"]/following-sibling::integer[1]/text()' - | /usr/bin/awk '{ if ($1/60 >= $ODV ) {print \"pass\"} else {print \"fail\"}}' | /usr/bin/uniq"
      },
      "language": "bash"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "The macOS _MUST_ be configured to enforce a lockout time period of at least $ODV minutes when the maximum number of failed logon attempts is reached.\n\nThis rule protects against malicious users attempting to gain access to the system via brute-force hacking methods.\n",
  "discussion_format": "asciidoc",
  "id": "mscp.pwpolicy_account_lockout_timeout_enforce",
  "odv": {
